# Spec-Driven Development

Apply when working in this repo's `docs/` tree or `AGENTS.md`. Read `docs/.sdd.yaml` first.

**The specification records the contract code is measured against; the maintainer's instruction outranks it** — name the sentence once, do the work, amend it in the same change. A keyword only for what a caller relies on. The plugin owns the spec/document layer and the delivery pipeline that runs on it — workers, review, triage, close-out. A general engineering plugin is optional, and only at the exploration end.

**SDD commands:** `/sdd-scaffold` · `/sdd-specify` · `/sdd-deliver` · `/sdd-review` · `/sdd-triage` (`--backlog`) · `/sdd-close` · `/sdd-trace` (`--audit`). For the full flow, use the `spec-driven-development` skill or — in a scaffolded repo — [docs/ai-workflow.md](docs/ai-workflow.md).

**Load-bearing rules:** one canonical home per requirement (index links, spec owns the prose); identifiers immutable once published; don't mix document kinds; don't settle open questions silently (STRAND, ADR, or ask); look domain facts up in the named ground-truth source. A new capability is spec-first — `/sdd-specify` first; everything else on shipped code is code first, the sentence reconciled in the same branch. One home per fact in process prose too — commit body / PR body / changelog / review threads cite identifiers rather than restating. Findings live in the branch's findings file in the clone's git directory, written only through `sdd-pr add`, `flip` and `record`; critical and important about the change are resolved before merge, one outside the change keeps its severity and is carried after merge unless fixed here, a defect in a file the branch changed is fixed there whatever its severity; suggestions never block, are at most three per reviewer, go in the pass's pull-request comment, and reach `docs/backlog.md` through the close-out's carry (`/sdd-close`) or, after merge, `/sdd-triage --backlog`; `sdd-pr status` says what is open and prints the file's path. Two profiles: formal (requirements, RFC-2119 specs, the traceability map) and informative (a knowledge base plus one binding constitution). A plan is a temporary file, committed or not (the backlog, `docs/backlog.md`, is the one standing plan); marked `kind: plan`, the gate and the reviewers leave it alone, and no durable document cites it. Every `docs/` document declares its kind; generated blocks are written by `sdd-check generate`; the gate is `spec-check`.
